# tests/infra/harness-layout-baseline.manifest
#
# GRANDFATHER BASELINE (the C2 ratchet) for the harness-layout contract —
# task #5265, PRD docs/prds/merge-gate-compile-cost.md §5 C1/C2, leaf B1.
# Read by tests/infra/test_harness_kloc_cap.sh (rule (b), "no re-accretion").
#
# FORMAT: one repo-relative `crates/<crate>/tests/<file>.rs` path per line.
# Comment lines (^\s*#) and blank lines are ignored (same stripping style as
# run-all-classification-lib.sh).
#
# WHAT IT LISTS: every top-level standalone `tests/*.rs` across the 5
# CONSOLIDATABLE crates (reify-cli, reify-syntax, reify-kernel-occt,
# reify-eval, reify-compiler) that is currently sanctioned by grandfathering.
# On the current pre-consolidation tree these are the un-consolidated
# standalone integration binaries; the guard treats a baseline-listed file as
# sanctioned so it is GREEN today, while a stray un-grandfathered file is
# flagged immediately.
#
# INTENTIONALLY EXCLUDED (never listed here):
#   - the 7 override binaries (determinism, analytical_validation,
#     modal_benchmarks, buckling_smoke, fea_diagnostics_e2e, tensegrity_t0a,
#     representation_within_assertion) — allow-listed by stem in the guard;
#   - any `harness_<subsystem>.rs` — governed by the kLOC cap (rule (a)), not
#     the re-accretion rule.
#
# THIS IS A RATCHET, NOT A PERMANENT ALLOW-LIST. Each consolidation leaf
# REMOVES its now-consolidated files from this baseline IN THE SAME DIFF that
# consolidates them (mirroring the mandatory same-diff
# run-all-classification.manifest row rule; esc-4914-162). The baseline shrinks
# leaf-by-leaf and the guard stays green at every intermediate step; shrinking
# toward empty == consolidation progress. Grandfathering a NEW row here for a
# new standalone test binary in one of these 5 crates is SUPERSEDED (Leo
# 2026-07-22, esc-5056-11: "actually start using the ratchet") — this baseline
# is a shrinking ratchet, not an allow-list to grow. The sanctioned remedy is
# consolidating the new test into a harness_<subsystem>/ compile unit, per C1;
# see scripts/check-harness-baseline-registration.sh's _hint() for the exact
# remediation wording (single source of truth — do not restate it here).
#
# REGENERATE (from repo root) — regenerate-and-DIFF, never regenerate-and-
# replace, and NEVER "check the count is unchanged": a ratchet only shrinks, so
# an unchanged count across a consolidation leaf is the bug, not the check.
#   git ls-files -- 'crates/reify-cli/tests/*.rs' 'crates/reify-syntax/tests/*.rs' \
#       'crates/reify-kernel-occt/tests/*.rs' 'crates/reify-eval/tests/*.rs' \
#       'crates/reify-compiler/tests/*.rs' \
#     | grep -E '/tests/[^/]+\.rs$' \
#     | grep -vE '/tests/(tensegrity_t0a|representation_within_assertion|harness_[^/]+)\.rs$' \
#     | sort
#
# `diff` that output against this file's data rows. In steady state they match
# EXACTLY, because the guard pins BOTH directions: a live standalone with no row
# fails rule (b), and a row with no live file fails the orphan-row scan in
# tests/infra/test_harness_kloc_cap.sh. A mismatch is therefore actionable — it
# is never a prompt to re-baseline this file wholesale:
#   listed here, absent from the output -> ORPHAN row: the file was consolidated
#     and its row was not removed. Delete the row (the consolidating leaf owed
#     it in the same diff).
#   in the output, absent here -> a NEW un-grandfathered standalone. Consolidate
#     it per C1; do NOT add a row — growing this baseline is superseded, above.
#
# HISTORICAL, NOT MAINTAINED — the first snapshot, kept only to date this
# baseline's origin: on base commit e6595a38 it was reify-cli 73, reify-syntax
# 61, reify-kernel-occt 48, reify-eval 395, reify-compiler 290 = 867 total.
# Landed consolidation leaves have shrunk it far below that (and three of those
# five crates to zero rows). The LIVE count is whatever the recipe above prints,
# and the guard's row scans already report it (`rows=N`) — deliberately not
# restated here, so it cannot go stale again.
